## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree to them as both strict obligations and conditions to all your licenses.

## Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the software to do everything you might do with the software that would otherwise infringe the licensor's copyright in it for any permitted purpose. However, you may only distribute the software according to Distribution License and make changes or new works based on the software according to Changes and New Works License.

## Distribution License

The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to distribute copies of the software. Your license to distribute covers distributing the software with changes and new works permitted by Changes and New Works License.

## Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of the software from you also gets a copy of these terms or the URL for them above, as well as copies of any plain-text lines beginning with `Required Notice:` that the licensor provided with the software. For example:

> Required Notice: Copyright Yoyodyne, Inc. (http://example.com)

## Changes and New Works License

The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to make changes and new works based on the software for any permitted purpose.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software that covers patent claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that you would infringe by using the software.

## Noncompete

Any purpose is a permitted purpose, except for providing any product that competes with the software or any product the licensor or any of its affiliates provides using the software.

## Competition

Goods and services compete even when they provide functionality through different kinds of interfaces or for different platforms, devices, or system environments, or through different channels. A product that replaces, substitutes for, offers substantially similar features to, or performs the primary functions of the software or the licensor's or affiliate's product competes with it.

## New Products

If the licensor or any of its affiliates stops providing a product using the software, a product that competed with it does not compete with it anymore, starting from when the licensor or affiliate stopped providing it.

## Discontinued Products

If the licensor or any of its affiliates stops providing all products using the software, and does not resume providing any such product for twelve consecutive months, the noncompete restriction ends.

## Sales of Business

If the licensor or any of its affiliates sells its business or assets relating to the software or any product it provides using the software to another organization, the buyer succeeds to the licensor's rights and obligations under Noncompete, Competition, New Products, and Discontinued Products.

## Fair Use

Nothing in these terms reduces or restricts your rights under copyright law, including fair use, fair dealing, or similar statutory exceptions.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not grant any other licenses, explicit or implied. Without limiting that rule, these terms do not license any patent claims for making, having made, using, offering to sell, selling, or importing any hardware, or any portion of any hardware, except as explicitly stated in Patent License.

## Patent Defense

If you institute or trigger patent litigation against the licensor or any of its affiliates, alleging that the software infringes any patent, your Patent License from the licensor ends automatically.

## Violations

The first time you are notified in writing by the licensor of any violation of these terms, or violate them without notice three or more times, all your licenses under these terms end automatically. If that happens, you must destroy all copies of the software you have.

## No Liability

As far as the law allows, the software comes as is, without any warranty, and the licensor will not be liable to you for any damages, under any legal theory, relating to the software or your use of it.

## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity that offers these terms, and **software** is the software the licensor makes available under these terms.
